title: Fundraising
new-page: true
view-if: fundraising_timer <= 0 and (not historical_mode)
on-arrival: fundraising_timer = 12
frequency: 300
is-card: true
card-image: img/Mann_der_Arbeit.jpg
tags: party_affairs

= Fundraising

To finance our party's operations, we receive donations from wealthy industrialists and dues from party members. To ensure a steady supply of funds, we must carefully balance our policies to avoid alienating our industrialist and labor factions. For convenience, we collect our funds at the end of each year and can adjust them throughout. 

- @maintain: Maintain our current funding.
- @reduce: Reduce dues.
- @increase: Request more funds.

@maintain
subtitle: [+ dues + industrial_funds +] resources will be collected.

We maintain our current dues.

@reduce
subtitle: [+ dues + industrial_funds - 1 +] resources will be collected.
unavailable-subtitle: Our grassroots fundraising is already low.
choose-if: dues > 1
on-arrival: dues -= 1; nationalist_dissent -= 8; industrialist_dissent -= 8; liberal_dissent -= 8; labor_dissent -= 8; democratic_dissent -= 8; progressive_dissent -= 8; month_actions += 1

Our current members appreciate this, but no one decides to join a party because of the low dues.

@increase
subtitle: [+ dues + industrial_funds + 1 +] resources will be collected. +1 resource [? if unemployed >= 15 : Given the present economic situation, this may be painful. ?][? if dues >= 4 : Dues are already rather high; increasing them might reduce our membership. ?]
view-if: (dues < 5 and labor_dvp == 1) or (industrial_funds < 5 and industrialists_dvp == 1) or dues < 2 or industrial_funds < 2

From whom should we request more funding?

- @industrialists: The industrialists
- @party_members: Our party members

@industrialists
subtitle: We shall request more resources from our industrial backers
unavailable-subtitle: [? if industrial_funds = 5: Their donations are already too generous in their mind ?][? if (industrial_funds = 2 and industrialists_dvp == 0): Many wealthy industrialists have left us to find another home for their interests in other right-wing parties ?].
choose-if: (industrial_funds < 5 and industrialists_dvp == 1) or industrial_funds < 2
on-arrival: industrial_funds += 1; resources += 1; industrialist_dissent += 5; month_actions += 1

Our wealthy backers complain about our rising expenses. Still, this doesn't affect our electoral performance and we have access to additional resources. 

@party_members
subtitle: We shall increase dues
unavailable-subtitle: [? if dues = 5: Dues are already as high as we can make them ?][? if (dues = 2 and labor_dvp == 0): With the defectionof our labor faction, raising dues beyond the current level is impossible ?].
choose-if: (industrial_funds < 5 and industrialists_dvp == 1) or industrial_funds < 2
on-arrival: dues += 1; resources += 1; new_middle_dvp -= 3; unemployed_dvp -= 3; new_middle_dvp -= 10 if unemployed >= 15; unemployed_dvp -= 10 if unemployed >= 15; new_middle_dvp -= 3*dues if dues >= 5; unemployed_dvp -= 3*dues if dues >= 5; month_actions += 1

Our members grumble at this, and some of the less committed members leave. But now, we have access to additional resources. 

[? if unemployed >= 15 : Because of the presently high unemployment, our members are feeling the extra burden hard. ?]

